Line	Meaning	Example
1	Number of instances	210
2	Number of item types in an instance	40
3	Bin/stock dimensions	100 × 100
4   onwards	Item data	40 rows per instance

The five columns represent:
Column	Parameter	Meaning
1	\(l_i\)	Length of item \(i\)
2	\(w_i\)	Width of item \(i\)
3	\(P_i\)	Minimum number of items of type \(i\)
4	\(Q_i\)	Maximum number of items of type \(i\)
5	\(v_i\)	Value of item \(i\)

The original problem is the constrained two-dimensional non-guillotine cutting problem.

The objective is to select and position rectangular items inside a single stock rectangle.